<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Portman returns to net profit in 1996.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Portman returns to net profit in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating loss			 0.93 vs loss 1.80</p>
<p>    Net profit			     4.53 vs loss 3.98</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	     4.0  vs nil</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	     4.0  vs nil</p>
<p>    Sales				   46.78 vs 41.89</p>
<p>    Other income			  19.93 vs  1.50</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    4.35 vs nil</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	     profit  5.46 vs loss 2.18</p>
<p>Dividend is franked to 3.46 cents  </p>
<p>Pay date Apr 2</p>
<p>Reg date Mch 17</p>
<p>    Tax					 nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Interest				 0.77 vs 0.85</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   3.58 vs 4.03</p>
<p>    Minorities				nil vs nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Portman Mining Ltd is a coal and iron ore miner. The net profit and dividend was the first in four years. Abnormal profit mainly comprised profit on the sale of the Pilbara manganese project and realised foreign exchange gains.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
